usamts-2016-r3-01.prompt:
Fill in each square of the $4\times 4$ grid with a number from 1 to 16, using each number exactly once. Numbers at the left or top give the largest sum of two numbers in that row or column. Numbers at the right or bottom give the largest difference of two numbers in that row or column.

The clues in the figure are:

* top (largest sum in columns 1–4): 13, 28, 25, 23;
* left (largest sum in rows 1–4): 13, 28, (none), 23;
* right (largest difference in rows 1–4): 7, (none), 8, 8;
* bottom (largest difference in columns 1–4): 7, (none), 12, 12.

You do not need to prove that your answer is the only one possible; you merely need to find an answer that satisfies the constraints above.
